
## Python-Specific

### Architecture
<!-- setup.sh replaces this based on detection -->
- **Framework:** {{PYTHON_FRAMEWORK}} <!-- Django / FastAPI / Flask / None -->
- **API style:** {{API_STYLE}} <!-- REST / GraphQL / gRPC -->
- **Async:** {{ASYNC_MODE}} <!-- yes/no -->

### Key Paths

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/` or `app/` | Application code |
| `tests/` | Test suite |
| `migrations/` or `alembic/` | Database migrations |
| `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml` | Dependencies |
| `config/` or `settings.py` | Configuration |

### Testing
- **Framework:** {{TEST_FRAMEWORK}} <!-- pytest / unittest -->
- **Run all:** `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`
- **Run specific:** `{{TEST_COMMAND}} <path>`
- **Run with coverage:** `{{TEST_COMMAND}} --cov`

### Style
- **Linter:** Ruff (`ruff check .`) or flake8
- **Formatter:** Ruff (`ruff format .`) or Black (`black .`)
- **Type check:** `mypy .` or `pyright`

### Python Conventions
- **Type hints:** Use type hints for all function signatures and return types
- **Imports:** Use absolute imports. Group: stdlib, third-party, local (separated by blank lines)
- **Exceptions:** Catch specific exceptions — never bare `except:`
- **Context managers:** Use `with` for file handles, DB connections, locks
- **Dataclasses/Pydantic:** Prefer dataclasses or Pydantic models over plain dicts for structured data
- **Async:** Use `async/await` for I/O-bound operations in async frameworks (FastAPI, aiohttp)

### Django Gotchas (if applicable)
- **N+1 queries:** Always use `select_related`/`prefetch_related` for associations in loops
- **Migration safety:** Never remove fields in the same deploy that removes code references
- **Forms/Serializers:** Validate all user input through forms (Django) or serializers (DRF)
- **Settings:** Use `django-environ` or similar — never hardcode secrets
- **Signals:** Avoid `post_save` for side effects — use service functions or tasks instead

### FastAPI Gotchas (if applicable)
- **Dependency injection:** Use `Depends()` for shared logic (auth, DB sessions)
- **Pydantic models:** Define request/response schemas — never return raw dicts
- **Background tasks:** Use `BackgroundTasks` or Celery for heavy work
- **Async DB:** Use async ORM (SQLAlchemy async, Tortoise) with async endpoints

### Database
- **ORM:** {{ORM}} <!-- Django ORM / SQLAlchemy / Tortoise -->
- **Migrate:** `python manage.py migrate` or `alembic upgrade head`
- **Rollback:** `python manage.py migrate <app> <previous>` or `alembic downgrade -1`
